        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_l_64_nfe-000977",
        "text": "Six Buccaneers have contributed to the practice squad and two are expected to be maintained. Packers tight ends Marshawn Johnson and Ryan Jackson are expected to remain in the squad. Browns wing Ryan Archer and Buccaneers defensive tackle Eddie Bosh are expected to return to the squad. Cleveland Cavaliers running back Steve OPodesta is one of the three running backs expected to remain on the practice squad. Green Bay Packers running back Tony Supman will return to the squad after having surgery for a sprained ankle. Orlando Magic tight ends Philip Nelson and Kid Williams are expected to resume practice. Orlando Magic defensive tackle Walter Bell is one of three players expected to make the practice squad. Packers cornerback Shaun Ortiz is also on the practice squad. (Photo: AP) Indiana coach John Kromier said in a release he still remembers six years ago he was about to conduct a simulation and cannot remember the job he thought he was going to do. On Monday, Kromier told The Sentinel that a simulation conducted by Indiana engineers must be ready in time for the annual \"Gemies of the Exams\" event, which will pit Tennessee against Arizona on Nov. 14. On Monday, Kromier said in a release he still has no memories of the simulations he was about to conduct. Six years ago, he saw computer video of a simulation conducted at Indiana's Penn Field facility, he said. He first noticed it on Dec. 23, 2013, while a student at the Indiana State University in Wichita. \"I can’t remember seeing computer video of a simulation,\" Kromier said. Indiana has a computer about five feet tall, but Kromier said one of the simulations, which is called Spikeplot 2.0, was conducted by a team looking to better coach young players. \"It’s kind of a new way to do your job,\" Kromier said of the simulation. When asked whether the move was temporary, he added, \"It looks like it’s going into a separate stage.\" Offensive lineman Kyle McKenning is dropping out of practice and offensive lineman Taaren Takkai and outside linebacker John Joseph were recruited as coaches. Quarterback Harris Dickey Jr. will now be on the practice squad when he retires, University officials said. Detroit Lions geare up to face off against the Bengals on Sunday for an AFC Division I regular season playoff game kick-off starting at 9 p.m.. Aaron Goldman of NFL Insider reported Friday afternoon that tight ends Shaun Thompson and center Brandon Morris, along with a host of Lions pass-rushing and interior offensive linemen, will feature in Sunday's second game in the AFC Division II regular season playoff with a warm-up starting at 9 p.m. The Lions, who should return to practice before No. 2, open the game Nov. 10 to face off against the Giants, Titans, and Hurricanes. Later in the game, Lions coach Ryan LaBlance asked QB Kaeper Becker if his defense has been better since the second half when the Lions took a 17-14 lead over the Bengals on Thursday. During the game, LaBlance said \"it's comes down to how well we know how to play. We have to be better on the field in terms of offenses.\" He also made a point to ESPN postseason analyst Chris Robertson: 2 interceptions and 41-yard passing losses isn't as bad as the game in Seattle. It's a lot better than the match against the Packers. — NFL Insider (@WRL insider) August 28, 2016 Robertson pointed to Lions QB Connie LaBlance: \"Let's get on with it.\" pic.twitter.com/pVVjywJZ5p — NFL Insider (@TICL) August 28, 2016 On the opening play, Lions QB Brandon Martin threw Texans running back Kelvin Mills for a touchdown passing loss and accused Texans defensive lineman Dean Kaepernick of doing \"the right thing.\" For a punt return-over, Martin opened the play by kicking tight end Jason Holiday of the Giants for a 43-yard passing loss and accusing Bengals defensive lineman Kaepernick of doing the wrong thing. The Lions played in the NFC championship game against the Red Bay Packers, the 2014 Super Bowl champion, in Kansas City, Mo and were using that match for the second time this postseason. Martin was unable to record previous Lions punt return-overs from his opponent. Video:"
