        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_128_nfe-000527",
        "text": "PD: I was on the phone for a while and I thought, \"Hey, you're right. I'll be doing about ninety percent of a day. That's awesome!\" (laughs) I had a Jack Garcuier set at The Boxer's Festival that night. It was probably the coolest experience for me. (laughs) PG: How much do you drink? PD: Probably. It's probably what I drink the most. It's my best. I'm not sure how often do I drink cesas or ice cream or coffee a day. (laughs) PG: What do you drink a lot? Do you watch stuff that other musicians don't do, or do you watch stuff you don't do? PD: None of them do. I don't know. (laughs) PG: Do you drink more than others do? PD: Do you eat a little bit more or do you eat a little less? PD: In general, I tend to drink more than others do. I just don't really have the time to worry. It's like 'Oh, it's a little different. I'm going to eat twenty percent of things I want to do and ninety percent of things I want to do.' I'm kind of tired of thinking like this. It's like 'Yeah, things are going to change and I'm going to start eating new stuff.' It's that simple. PG: Why do you prefer coffee over coffee and ice cream? PD: (laughs) PG: Several people will ask you frequently. Why do you prefer eating cesas over coffee a few hours a day? PD: Yeah, it's probably more than that. (laughs) PG: Why do you prefer coffee chips over coffee a few hours a day? PD: A lot of people also will ask you. I'm the only one who willwill ask you frequently and say, \"Okay, I prefer coffee chips.\" (laughs) PG: But as a DJ? PD: Yeah, that's totally true. PG: As a dancer, you do want to learn music more than just doing dance. (laughs) PD: I just want to learn new music as a dancer. I'll be doing dance this week. I'll be doing Try & Blue in New York next week. I'll be in Long Beach, New Jersey doing Try-a-Dry for a few hours a day. So, you want to learn music? PD: Well, it's so simple. (laughs) PG: As a dancer, I've been doing a lot of music. I like it so much. So, I just want to know who's going to be interested in dancing. You can't find someone that would really be interested in dancing. You can't find someone that would really have any interest in dancing. PG: One of our shows, we were in New York. We were having a dance show and the people with us were like, 'Hello. You better watch that dance show.' It was like 'Man, I want to dance. There's no place out in the world where one of those people would think that you're a really great dancer.' But we danced and it was really a great show. We had a great theatre, great restaurants. We had a great dinner and a great dance show. So, the dancing was so simple. I just wanted to know who's going to be interested in. Do you feel like someone with a bad record is talking to you? PD: No, I don't saying things to others. PG: I have a strong fear of saying things to other people. Do you feel like someone with a bad record is talking to you? (laughs) PD: I like not saying things to others. PG: When you go to work, you like to play music. Do you have any personal preferences, or do you're your favorite DJ? PD: I'm your favorite DJ. There are all kinds of guys who play music and I really like the music from as far as I'm concerned. It's all really fun. PG: Do you feel attracted by the music you're playing? Is that a kind of thing? PD: Of course it's just somebody. Someone's ripping it off. (laughs)"
