        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-000163",
        "text": "A: The artists that I was looking for weren't very talented in the '90s. They weren't very talented, though, which is what I was always looking for. I used to take pictures of my kids at work. I would take pictures of my kids at school and at parties with my friends. I would go home and get a picture, and until that point, they were medium-sized and very small. I did want, for a while, to experiment with a different style of photography, but, in the build up to the ‘90s, I didn't have the resources for a high quality photography. The artists that I was looking for were actually very talented. Q: What's it like to head out on a vacation and learn more about the art history of your country? A: I've spent a lot of time studying the archives. I've visited different places, and I started learning more and more about the arts in particular in the '90s. And there are a lot of reasons why I want to visit the arts. For historians, you can see them all over the country. You can see the Museum of Ethnic Arts. For travelers to America, you can see the National Museum of Electronic Arts or the Museum of Education Photography, among other things, and you can find them from all over the country. And you can find a lot of them in other countries. Q: Living in close proximity to the arts, what's it like to live in such close proximity to the arts? A: I started out as a kid. I'd hang out with friends in my house. They'd get pictures whenever if they wanted, and I'd take pictures of monkeys and apes and follow along. That's where I wanted to be. When I first moved to New York, I felt a very close connection to the arts and I felt a deep connection to the arts. Q: If you've dedicated your time to learning about photography, what's your favorite thing about photography? A: I was just watching Dan [Gabhausen]'s radio show, The Dan Gabhausens Show, when one of my students asked me about good photography. She gave me a 30mm camera and sliced it into an oil pot, and then some oil. She turned to me and said, ‘Oh, can you learn more about photography?' I'm not really worried about that. I really like the idea of good photography for shooting. The kids just ran away from it, and for a while, I threw it away. And I threw it away and did various things. I was in college, and I really improved on a lot of things. If I was really interested in photography, I'd walk out in my apartment car and take the picture. If I can do that, I have to pay more attention to capturing it and focusing on it, and I just really like it. It's probably my favorite. Q: What's the difference between borrowing on photography and borrowing out of banks? A: I only borrow out of banks. When I was doing photography, I only borrow out of banks. It's really not as easy as I thought. I lived a little bit differently without banks, and I did different things, and I just lived completely differently. The bank giants would bail me out of this; if they didn't bail me out, I would start taking cash and taking off. I became a banker. Q: Is it true that Time Warner and other media giants have a similar type of borrowing approach that they used to in the past? A: In some cases, they have taken a different approach. For example, I think that borrowing works much more closely and follow the same path many bankers do when trying to provide photography. if it's this type of image, it's taken into place; if it's a big, beautiful, detailed image, it's put into place from day one. Q: How important do you decide which image you want? A: These are very important things. You have to be able to provide photography at the highest quality, to have people easily related to them on your site. These are also things that people have to take into account, whether they buy an image or put it on auction. Right now, you don't have to spend big money on something just to get it. You can do it through the internet; you can also do it in a variety of ways depending on the image you choose. You can travel it, you can buy and sell it and see it in the media and in movies, you can send photography to a specific location, you can turn an image into a film, you can shoot it."
