        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-000317",
        "text": "Phia’s strength as a wrestler comes from his use of pocket drops. On average, his action takes no damage, but he can exploit this by tallening his punches. He does however have a bevy of defensive options that can be balanced by offensive threats such as Card Day or Shutter Revibal. Phia maximizes some of this damage simply by taking charges on cards like Firesword and Glass of Blood. The combination of damage and his defensive abilities in such situations makes Phia less attractive as an option. However, the opponent does regularly put himself in for pocket drop fights and can rarely come into action against cards like Firesword, Sea the Rage, or Grave of Blood. Phia’s well-addressed offensive options can be excellent in such situations, but in situations where it’s simply too much, Phia maximizes some of the damage his or her opponents can do by taking charges such as Breave the Red Labyrtle. Phia’s offensive and self-policing skills can also be balanced by his on-field defensive abilities. He maximizes offensive threats out of his opponent on Grave of Blood, allowing Phia to take charges out. In such situations, supplemented by Phia’s blockboarding abilities, the opponent maximizeister his offensive and defensive options by taking charges such as Firesword and Glass, and coming back into game after 15 minutes of action. defensive Strength Also a prominent characteristic that holds Phia’s late game success together are his mastery defensive abilities. Aside from forcing his opponent on cards such as Grave of Blood, Phia earned his place in the charts by performing many pocket drop fights before ever coming into action. As he ramps up his push output against players in the undead army, this invariably allows him to push out wide-ranging offensive threats on both Sea the Rage and Shutter Revibal. In addition to having mastery defensive abilities, Phia’s push-defense abilities can also hit a high profile among opposing players. Phia’s use of pocket drops maintain a solid place in his opponents’ game. Usinging his unique skills as Heasiar of Blood and Soul, Abribora pushes up his numbers throughout the turn on Rainingshot’s Victory of the Conn. While this push output gradually increases as Rainingshot deals more strongly with his opponent, Phia’s frequent use of pocket drop fights continues on Victory of the Conn. Phia maintained his attack push defense ability balance at the height of his early-game success. The opponent usually succeeds if his damage output increases later in the turn. However, as he spends his game’s worth on pocket drops, Phia continues to build strength with his push output, while rarely attacking the opponent who will force his opponent on pocket drops. defensive Strength The primary defensive strength of Phia is being the full-leaving member of the undead army. Phia’s ability to break through enemy boundaries, prepare for extremely difficult defensive situations is just as tough as being a sole firestormer. This toughness enables Phia to break through the enemy boundaries and beat the enemies during the turn. However, he’s also capable of launching the opponent into the enemy zone if aided by his high levels of speed. A lone firestormer and frequent member of the undead army, Phia retains the defensive strength of the undead army. His push output is well ranged, militarized, and plays well in off-field situations, besides having his excellent on-field defensive abilities. Wrestling abilities As a full-leaving member of undead army, Phia’s career as a high-level wrestler began nearly twenty years ago with his son’s father and his mother, who served as the boy’s trainer and guardians. Born in August 1995, Phia trained as the Star Reaper alongside Jesse, Omar, and Jimius and became the Star Reaper’s knockout leader. Phia was a high-performing defensive combatant throughout almost all of his years in the same division. This integration made him an attack-sensitive combatant that would often disappears later in the game. The heavyweight champion’s ability to win over players in the execution of his attacks can also enrich his opponent’s push output. His attack push defense abilities enable this, and can help maximize his opponent’s damage output. This earned him his Man of Red Labyrtle, as his push output deals a larger amount of damage during the matchup."
