        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-000817",
        "text": "In addition to the Philadelphia Eagles podcast, for the 2015 Philadelphia vs. Arizona State Pacers match on Saturday (10 a.m. – 9 p.m. at Wembley Field), sign up for the podcast, \"Palen Chat,\" and get an on-demand $10 free membership. Philadelphia fans are eligible for the weekly Philadelphia Eagles podcast and will watch the match on social media, as well as live coverage of the match via the video app. The podcast is also popularly called \"Palen Chat.\" For the 2015 Philadelphia vs. Arizona State Pacers match, hear the Philadelphia Eagles Podcast chat on your homestand. The membership is not renewed for a month. To sign up for the podcast, go to the studio and call 1-365-708-8677 (loge-in at a minimum or opt-out). The membership is not renewed for a month. Philadelphia fans are eligible for the Philadelphia Eagles podcast and will watch the match on social media, as well as live coverage of the match via the video app. For more information on the podcast program, can be found here. hear the Philadelphia Eagles Podcast chat on your homestand and get an on-demand free membership. To sign up for the podcast, go to the studio and call 1-365-708-8677. Buy Photo Philadelphia Eagles defensive tackle Nick Hardberg. Courtesy AP \"He is a legend in Philadelphia,\" Eagles head coach Greg Giancarino said. \"He'll be in there and wait until he gets his chance.\" Hardberg, a two-year veteran with 118 tackles and sacks in 10 games, leads the Eagles with 35.26 career tackles per game. At 3-5.1, the Eagles rank second in career tackles with an NFL average of 29.59. \"He wants to produce at the right rate and he's shown that to us,\" Giancarino said. \"He has great movement on the defensive end and he's got a good sense of how to get out there to play. He also does a great job of helping the team win on the defensive end.\" Zach Johnson set a career high with 67 tackles in 41 games during his rookie season, while Max Houghton, who played for the Minnesota Vikings on Saturday night last week, leads the Eagles with 58 tackles in 16 games. \"He's the best tackle in the NFL and he definitely has a good sense of winning,\" Johnson said. \"He also does a great job of performing on the defensive end. He's got good movement, he's got good attitude on the defensive end and he's going to help the Eagles win.\" Still, Giancarino said, the Eagles' new defensive linemen need to build on Hardberg's progress and be strong in their numbers in order to continue to count on Hardberg to step up to the defensive end. \"I think Nick's athleticism is there. To strengthen that, we just need to build up the offensive line to run the ball,\" Johnson said. \"We see a lot of guys who are in really good possessions on the defensive side of the ball playing. So he'll be in there and we're counting on him to step up on the defensive end.\" Update 1/11: This article's version says a release date for Hardberg has gone to the Eagles. Details have yet to be released. Authorities said a man was injured in the downtown Phoenix neighborhood Thursday morning following a shooting at a house in the 300 block of North Allen Avenue. The man, 25 years old, was standing on the second floor of the house at 11:30 a.m. when the shot was fired, but the man did not suffer an injury and was taken to Channo UHR Medical Center. The suspect is still being held, said Phoenix Police Sgt. Michael Geinrich. The man’s injury comes three days after a shooting at an apartment in the 4300 block of North Allen Avenue, which has been a frequent occurrence in the neighborhood. Four suspects and three women were arrested in downtown Phoenix on Thursday, Geinrich said. “Everyone is encouraged to call the police and help them get information quickly. Things like this rarely happen in Phoenix,” Geinrich said. “It’s kind of a contrast to the early 1990s, when there were a lot of unarmed women who were sexually abused in our neighborhood.” A 39-year-old neighbor, Geinrich said, said he was confronted by the man with a firearm and told her he was trying to get inside her house. While outside, the man pulled out the firearm and shot at his neighbor."
