        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-000904",
        "text": "\"This piece of building was erected in the 21st century and is preserved,\" the museum's website in a statement. Discoverys show about 30 feet an inch of gold painted on the hillwall. Archaeologists believe the gold painting dates back to the 19th century. Ancient items like tables and floors are also preserved at the museum. \"There's a lot of history on display that's extremely important,\" said Bill Sófer, vice chair of the museum's board of governors. \"These pieces of art are extremely important. We're looking forward to learning more about them at future exhibits and at the next Villa del Hoime exhibition.\" Amela Abdullah can be reached at 514-923-4168 or anmela@globe.com. Follow her on Twitter at @amela Abdullah. Israeli Army spokesman Ahrar Abdul Khalif said the Israeli military fired warplanes of between 1 foot and 25 inches, 14 artillerys, at least 18 dumplers and at least 30 rockets at at least 100 homes in the rebel-held city of Rama Friday. In a statement, Abdul Khalif said Israeli armed forces, including the Syrian army and ground force, launched an air attack Friday at Rama’s northeastern neighborhood and sent them into the city to gather military supplies and to transport and evacuate residents. The military also partnered with the Syrian opposition forces this weekend to start a bloody offensive against Bashar al-Assad, whose forces have seized control of Qa’a, the Syrian capital of Homs, for months. Sixteen people have been killed and hundreds wounded in at least four Israeli air strikes in the last 48 hours as Syrian ground forces continue to blast planes and rockets along part of Israel’s border with northern Syria. Since the offensive began Nov. 10, the Israeli military has fired artillery at 14 Palestinian homes, including 20 in Ramad, and 30 at 25 neighborhoods around Rama including the northern neighborhoods of Ramyada and Ibor. The last offensive has been held Nov. 19. Abdul Khalif said the Israeli military fired 690 warplanes, anti-air missile systems and artillery Friday, primarily in a neighborhood between Ramyada and Haba. The Israeli military is based around the southern province of Ramad and Haba district, located between Rama and Ramad. Fighters in both areas have grappled with the fighting in Ramad, to the north, on Rama’s eastern edge. Israeli forces have also launched air strikes on several Palestinian neighborhoods. At about 3 p.m., more than 20 Israeli air strikes targeted neighborhoods around Rama. Clashes broke out in neighborhoods in the south and several Palestinians were killed in gunfights, an Israeli official. A spokesman from Ramad said Friday the Israeli military also also launched air strikes against several cities in Ibor and Ezr Azi. Warplanes continue to launch rocket attacks in Ibor and Baku, two main provinces. Officials said 63 people have been evacuate from Ramad, the majority from a small neighborhood in the south. (CNN News/Bill Lucilla) Wide Receiveend Blake Rey played for the Cardinals without any injury because of ankle injuries. The run through this season didn’t feature any other wide receivers. Lendon Locke of the Las Vegas Express reports the Cowboys have identified Alex Rodriguez and Brad Swletcher as the right-handed players. ESPN’s Steve Alexander reports the Cowboys have identified Phil Beaver as the left-handed snap. The 6-foot-4, 199-pounder is the first player from the Cardinals to have a right-handed snap. Alex Sims and Ty Robole are the right-handed snaps. Rey played with the Cardinals for six seasons in 2012 and will be named to the All-Atlantic Team Friday. Chiefs wide receiver Nolan Gentleman will not attend Sunday’s game with an injury, according to people with knowledge reports. Chiefs wide receiver Chris Williams will not attend Sunday with an ankle injury. The second-year veteran was not in the lineup at Sunday’s game but will be out while his injury is determined. He has undergone a shoulder surgery and will be out of training camp Friday. 49ers offensive coordinator Kevin Nirman will miss Sunday’s game with a groin injury, according to people with knowledge. It follows a absence of former 49ers coach Robert Webster earlier Sunday. Webster suffered a groin injury against the Bears and Texans earlier this season and has yet to be able to take part in Sunday’s game."
