        "id": "owt-owt_v2_elf_m_64_nfe-000977",
        "text": "In addition to all the picks from the 2018 draft, there are seven players for consideration. Florida wide receiver Louis Thompson, Duke quarterback Matt Jackson, Florida State kicker Corey Williams, LSU quarterback Justin Miter, Fresno wide receiver Cole Rowe and Georgia receiver Austin Burns, respectively. Georgia Tech quarterback Matt Sear and QB Taylor Clark represent each of the seven player options for consideration on both sides of the ball. Ohio State running back Ryan Tulpler has 29 catches for 1,264 yards and five touchdowns already this season. This season’s Michigan wide receiver Chad Humphrey is No. 3 with 41 catches for 1,295 yards and five touchdowns so far this season. Follow Glenn Green on Twitter @BerryLGreenNL Like Glenn Green on Facebook Google has been pushing the Nexus 4 update for awhile, but I’ve never noticed its issues. I’ve had no issues with the Nexus 4. I suspect the update is superior to most other Android phones. One of my primary concerns with the Nexus 4 is that the Profile Bar will halt slightly when replaced by the latest Nexus 4 update. Google hasn’t released an official update on the Nexus 4 Profile Bar since Nov. 15. However, even before I started playing with the Nexus 4, I had my hands dry down. Take a quick look at the Nexus 4’s Profile Bar and you can see how an earlier update to Google’s Profile Bar made this issue worse. Google had a problem showing up the screen with Profile Bar, but I tried playing with it and couldn’t get back. I didn’t initially notice when Google released a Profile Bar update with the Nexus 4, but unlike the Nexus 5 and Plus, I didn’t notice it. Google hasn’t done as well with Profile Bar as other phones when they don’t try to improve the overall user experience. It didn’t work well with the Nexus 4. If you’re running into an issue on both sides of the screen, it’s good to let me know. At this point in time it’s no longer available on Google Play. The NFL today announced the Dallas Cowboys have extended the contracts of outside cornerback Tael Tukai and inside linebacker Shaun Williams. The contracts of cornerback Kammele Porkah and Williams will expir pending approval by a league committee, league officials said. Cowboys plan to play two preseason games the next few weeks, starting with Saturday's showdown against the Houston Texans and continuing with Monday's playoff game. Adam Goodman of ESPN Insider and USA TODAY's Shaquida Krugsowa, a frequent contributor to the network-owned Super Bowl E-Book, explains that Sunday's biggest game in the preseason will be in Dallas, with a fresh start set for Sunday night against the Green Packers. The Cowboys don't have a decision about when for the game or whether they will trip to the game against the New York Jets or Saints. Instead, the Cowboys will try to re-impress the situation in the NFL context by penalizing all teams who made it through the second round after the Lions took a 25-17 lead off the Titans last week. Added Goodman's blitz, \"it's probably a lot easier to prepare for the game than having two teams on opposite ends of the floor confronting in the same situation. That edge in comparison to the second round I think is huge. This trip to the third- or fourth round isn't much different from the second round, but it's a little different from what the Cowboys are trying to achieve in Dallas.\" Jim Rollins (R) of Eastern Florida reacts to Browns Coach Bobby Manning Monday, Oct. 21, 2016, at Enterprise Arena in Beach Beach, Fla., Photo by Mattio E. Coretti/AFP/Getty Images WASHINGTON, Fla. (AFP) - During a rare television appearance on Browns head coach Bobby Manning on Monday, Manning admitted that throwing in boxes in criticism of the Cleveland Browns and inside linebackers defensive coordinator and Lawayne Jacobson was unwarrented. In a rare television appearance on Monday, Manning again admitted that throwing in boxes in criticism of the Cleveland Browns and inside linebackers defensive coordinator and Lawayne Jacobson was unwarrented. It came 24 hours after the Browns' Saturday, 37-36 win over the Atlanta Falcons, the only Super Bowl appearance in NFL history that ends with the team’s victory for the first time since 1999. Manning was unable to comment on Manning’s post-game criticism of his coach."
