        "text": "’ most expensive new acquisition for Manchester City since joining from Juventus last summer, remained with the club’s squad after the Champions League draw against Gaziedad. He is suspended for the rest of the season and had appeared in their last 11 as a substitute at Watford on 17 March when he scored both of his penalties but was deactivated when Guardiola abandoned that game. Mourinho decided against substituting Agüero from the European game and also revealed the 24-year-old had been struggling with weight and tightness. The City manager hoped Agüero would be available for Saturday’s trip to Chelsea when his team had played in Europe. “Right now, the main injury is in his thigh. If everything else is OK, he would then be ready for the next game at home when we are back from international break,” he said. Mourinho’s team were later beaten 5-0 on aggregate by Bosnia-Herzegovina in the Nations League and the team appeared visibly disappointed by the final whistle. Speaking after the game, though, Guardiola had stood by an impressive performance and had branded his side dominant in the early stages of the game. “You can rely on a really small number of players. We created so many chances. We could have created more at times, but I thought we were too negative and not intense enough,” Guardiola told reporters before leaving City early.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>Request Full Access Anlista Exclusive Report on industrial disinfectant processing from raw materials to manufacturers Introduction SUMMARY/BACKGROUND The increasing dynamics of rapid industrialization process, increased industrial output and rapidly changing commodity trends have paved the path for unprecedented high demands for disinfectant detergents across various industries. These specialized detergents such as disinfectants offer significant advantages over water resistant products in several industrial processes. Inert disinfectant products are resistant to drying, anoxia and cyanosis due to significant acidity changes in solvents and low concentration of water in activated or evaporated detergents in the drying process. Disinfectants are widely used in industrial industries such as chemical, pharmaceutical, waste, food, industrial and hold the most market-share in the global market. These industries exhibited significant growth during the past few years, and are expected to exhibit an enhanced growth trend to retain the dominant position in the very near future. In the market, share of Separate Disinfectant Products and Combined Disinfectant Products during the forecast period 2019 to 2025 is anticipated to witness growth of 5.43% to 6.60% on annual basis owing to increase of market presence. The overall market size is estimated to register an annualized growth of 3.92% until 2026. Moreover, the selectivity of the disinfectants subject to negligible temperature or high temperatures, as well as greater chemical stability achieved at processing time are the inherent advantages of such products as compared with others. Such disinfectants provide plant operators and manufacturers with a strong emphasis on quality and cost reduction approaches. Promoting innovative solutions is one of the factors responsible for the growth rate of disinfectants in the market. Hastily available raw materials and improved working procedure provide cost reduction to manufacturers. Utilization of disinfectants has been required to prevent water contamination in appliances, plastic equipment, rubber cloth can reduce moisture-related damage, toxicity and quality degradation in various applications. Food packaging has been one of the fastest growing industries in the world, but most of these products require a long shelf life with proper storage. However, high contamination rate in the storage of the packaged food products is one of the factors responsible for the growth prospect of disinfectants in this market. These products are widely used for production and packaging of packaged food products. Fragile water consumption, hygiene and food safety concerns are giving more importance to the end product. Producing high quality product in this market is difficult and often a step process, thus regular high quality testing is necessary to enhance the output. Easy production process is the major factor for promoting disinfectant market. SEARCH INFORMATION & SPECIFICATION Coverage Name Industrial Disinfectant Additive Market Regment, 2018 Million, US$ 13,514 million Report Title - Industrial Disinfectant Additive | Challenges to Innovations Analysis Company Size In-House A-Note Coverage Outlook Forecast Years, 2019 to 2025 SUMMARY MARKET REFERENCES :- Water Disinfectants, Water Cantevers, Repellents, Building & Construction, Stabilizers, Refrigeration Machinery, Medical & Pharmaceuticals, Food & Beverages, Liquor & Souvenirs, Mixing Containers, Electronics & Accessories, Auto & Motors, Franchises & Brands, Funeral Solutions Industrial Disinfectant Market Segment By Wet-walled Disinfectant Products (series), Separate Disinfectant Products (series), Combatile Disinfectant Products"
