        "id": "owt-owt_v2_plaid_4096_nfe-000466",
        "text": "The first map win the French managed against OpTic gave them immense confidence coming in to the event as both Quad Train and Dust 2 are two maps that EnVyUs have never played in the past. They were able to move on to the next map after a very good pistol round but the Americans showed a great double split to clutch a few rounds. If EnVyUs are able to achieve wins like this in the future then they will have a good chance of winning the tournament they want. Before moving on to the following map, the French squad took out their American counterparts in the final seconds of Legends Garden. While the American side was seemingly in a position to handle French Minor due to previous performances, EnVyUs somehow managed to keep their opposition inside a few rounds multiple times as their decision making stayed strong throughout the entire course of the match from start to finish. Had the Americans could have nabbed the win it would have been a massive achievement for EnVyUs as it was exactly the round that they needed. Once they had the round, EnVyUs star player Jilil “⁠jkaem⁠” Abadir came out and led the offense. He was unable to throw down any sort of big high order defense however he still came up with some great plays in a few instances. Not only was he able to take the win but also helped his side dominate the previous round. EnVyUs were actually able to play very well to hold on for the win this first map and they will need to pull out some rounds like this in future if the French side is going to spring a massive upset in London. Map 4-5: Dust2 - Dragon - Cobblestone The confidence of EnVyUs took a severe hit in the first two maps against Evil Geniuses as the French played a very good pistol round on Quad Train but lost several crucial rounds. Despite the few setbacks they led the offense very well against the American juggernaut in a strong 16-6 win in the first of three maps played. The second map in this match was definitely one of EnVyUs’s worst maps. Communication is a major factor that makes up and breaks a match against the best teams in the world. The French squad had never dealt with map pressure like this before and handled them well. The Europeans grinded out the victory to the tune of 11 rounds as William “⁠hazed⁠” Trachtenberg dominated the de_Mirage side and turned the rounds in their favor. The Americans managed to regain their lead later on with some great rounds and broke several of the European’s key spots on the map. They were able to pick off a few rounds while Bruno “⁠Shox⁠” Jiménez was still alive but the match featured some great performances from the North American team while James “⁠friberg⁠” Liprušek put his team toe-to-toe up against the best team in the world. Map 6: Red Country - De_Mirage - DustLake2 - De_Execution For the second time at the event, EnVyUs played against the best teams in the world but this time they went up against a Brazilian roster. The French side was ultimately unable to walk away with the victory as the Americans won the match 16-8 in the second of three maps played. That being said, the Brazilian team was not the best they would face as the likes of SK Gaming, FlipSid3, Astralis and G2 Esports were deadly in this matchup. The decision making from EnVyUs was great in this round as they were able to go through each side multiple times and not have lost one round. They were able to go for it multiple ways in back to back maps although in such matches you can’t have too much faith in EnVyUs’s aim. If the French side is going to contend in the competition, they will have to show the world how good their aim can be. Map 7: Red Country - Skullgirls - Double Dragon - Triple C4 Finally we get to the central map of FACEIT London, Plant Double Dragon. Very few teams would be able to win this legendary pistol round but EnVyUs nearly managed that. The Skullgirls managed to get themselves plenty of rounds in the first half and dominated from start to finish. While they did lose one round on the neutral side, EnVyUs were able nuke the win in their favor in the matter of just two rounds. The play from the North American side was amazing and it should be massive motivation for EnVyUs as they enter the tournament. If the team can bring anywhere close to this performance then the French squad will have a chance to go on a rampage and secure a spot in the playoffs of the FACEIT London 2018 Major. Map 8: Cob"
