        "text": "Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 The blind love you have for yourself is unsettling to me. The rage and visceral hate you have for your audience is inspiring to me. I’ll finish this thread with my next media show against – at my convenience and on your lunch break. Remember #HowToGet woke? — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Wait, I didn't know that. Erin. You have two choices. You can participate in the conversation by addressing the selfishness, or you can reject the entirety of the hate. pic.twitter.com/WGz0YdZ9dM — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Erin. Don't get offended. There's only you to apologize for. pic.twitter.com/DfGnv1rq4W — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Look who’s nice and not trying to be triggered and told what to write about. pic.twitter.com/dRrN1YOQjA — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 It gets more complicated in closed proximity. You only have option 1. Start wearing the loudest looking skin imaginable. Pun intended. — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Everyone's bad, but engaging with bad people doens't condone a bad person. You're right, a big deal. and that emoji is scary. — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 You don’t have to be a hypocrite, OK? You don’t have to be responsible for the massive amounts of abomination you cause. The hair is disgusting too. Fuck these people. pic.twitter.com/1i65WcBY0x — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 I know it’s hard to look people who disagree with you in the eyes. But you're right, you're right. Yes, that was the big moment. pic.twitter.com/NYHLj3Yo3N — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 I saw it. It was hard. A sad part is that I didn't manage it well. \"Done well\" means \"understand the context\", \"stay calm in the situation & not to nitpick,\" — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 And while the conversation was not civil, it was polite and, in the end, it was productive, Erin. Che. pic.twitter.com/0bPGKKTKnw — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Don’t get me wrong, I think it’s important to watch a public media interview and learn from the host. @ErinkpnFlog is a great reporter and deserves conversation, but I want to share and leave this❤️❤️😺❤️❤️ pic.twitter.com/ABgz28p3jr — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 And I really like your new book, The Progressive Agenda. Politically Taming the Left is useful and funny, *pun intended.* pic.twitter.com/bLUExyXPv — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 This is a real moment between two real people who don’t hate each other. Next place I’m looking for a fight is with a racist bigot. Good luck. pic.twitter.com/DxjWUxapml — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Everyone's bad, but engaging with bad people doens't condone a bad person. It's just how too many people live their lives. — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 I may be surrounded by white privilege in white spaces, but I'm met with hate when I enter a white place, and I'm full of walls every time I go in anywhere. — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Personally, I likely enjoy a significant amount of hate-fueling white privilege. A white person has twice yelled at me. — Kate Toye (@KateToye) April 30, 2019 Wendy proudly asserts her white privilege against me. Dan empases me when I tell him he has white privilege. White folks, I love you for everything. But I don't always want it for you. — Kate Toye (@KateToy"
