        "id": "owt-owt_v2_plaid_4096_nfe-000634",
        "text": "a major boost in its resume on Monday. The pair’s economic narratives clashed sharply amid anxiety over the policy outlook in the United States. Warren used her speech to reaffirm her record on financial regulation, taking aim at Sanders for his decision to pursue a repeal of the Dodd-Frank financial reform. The battle was a rare turn for the long-time progressive Vermont senator, who has been able to push his progressive credentials early on in the race thanks to his strong backing from labor and progressive groups. New Jersey Sen. Cory Booker and former New York City Mayor Michael Bloomberg also gave speeches, but focused on the root causes of America’s economic woes. Booker called for criminal justice reform and highlighted gentrification in Baltimore and Chicago, as well as the nation’s historic rates of incarceration. The president released more than 1,500 inmates over the weekend. Yang criticized the leftward movement within the Democratic Party, taking a slight swipe at Bernie Sanders. The Vermont senator had surged to victory Saturday over Amy Klobuchar in the Nevada caucuses, prompting new personal debate questions to come from Yang. The businessman highlighted the ideological disagreements, specifically asking about Bernie Sanders’ place at the next Democratic presidential debate on Friday in Des Moines, Iowa. Democrat Pete Buttigieg used his speech to focus on the moderate wing of the Democratic Party. Buttigieg, who finished third in Iowa, criticized Biden, who held a nearly 20-point lead on Buttigieg in Iowa, for quoting an inordinate amount of his speech in the last week. “We need new voices and ideas,” he said. “My desire for a complete transformation of the party is not the direction Joe Biden wanted to take.” Though Biden’s primary race appeared to have eased slightly Monday night, his campaign continues to project strength as he looks to roll through the early primary states.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>We’ve got four new species to talk about this week, and we’ve got another four that we think you’ll want to see in the coming weeks. Let’s get to the list, shall we? New PvP Talents 1. Scattering Fern – It’s a perfect hedge for those windy days! 2. Basilclaw Vibricrapefern – This unique-looking shrub is the one you need this spring to add heft to your garden. Returning Extension Talents 3. Waterfall Balm – We’ve got a few perennials in our grove at home and we’d love to help you grow some! 4. Handcrop and Sunflowers – Good to remember when you need something colorful to plant in your hotbox. Returning Landscape Living Talents 1. Starlit Rainbow Lotorbera – Stars are bursting here left and right and this spiky, hybrid tree showcases them all. 2. Hetman Cyiola – This is a great hedge to relax in, and it’s the perfect size to hold a pineapple or orange. 3. Sakura Fukuashulps – Think of it as a caterpillar net, but with a real Sakura in it. UPDATE May 9, 2018: Remember what I said about taking care at the start of the Talents section from yesterday when I mentioned our lovely, helpful friends? We’ve got more exciting pets and plants coming this week with 1.4, but I’m sure you also want to check out the Seed updates and here’s a look at a few of the ones that have already been released into the game. Featured Garden Species 1. Silver Rock Polyfern – Do you really need a wheatflower when you’ve got this beautiful vine tree nearby? 2. Effervescent Floryslope – Trust me, I planted this garden so I’m sure you’ll want to prune this tree. 3. Impressive Mega Grown Heather – Yup, Jeppe totally upstaged me again this week. This is a survivor plant from our last seed update, and like any good survivor, it’s gained some popularity as of late. It also gives you options for your compost bin, kitchen counter, or as your own critter, perennials being available for harvesting is awesome! UPDATE May 9, 2018: I’m not sure Jeppe got my little jab at this plant here. Back during Alpha Testing, players would sometimes show off pictures of their tuggies of plants and it was a bit of a light-hearted joke. Mind you, he was rocking some serious canines for that picture. Perhaps it would’ve been a good idea to follow his lead up and stay out of my garden! We’ve got more exciting plants to introduce and are planning on showing off during the next update and we hope to tell you about more as we’re able"
