        "id": "owt-owt_v2_plaid_4096_nfe-000903",
        "text": ", we wanted to allow users to edit marks on the map. We already mentioned that by default Ralc made coordinate updates. Yet, we thought that it would really be better if we allowed users to rename the marks and give the option to edit them too. It would be even better if you could just put your own marks on the map and then edit them elsewhere on Sailfish as well. That’s when we came up with the idea of special keystrokes to edit the marker on any of the map nodes. As already mentioned, this is not going to be perfect in the long term. But for now editing the map will hopefully be less of a hassle for users. Here is what the new keystroke does look like: Press Ctrl-T to put the map in navigation Press Ctrl-X to go to the next coordinate on the map Press Ctrl-D to go to a coordinate of interest (hidden in the map) Press Ctrl-L to mark that point on the map Press Ctrl-J to create a point on the map Press Ctrl-A to edit a point of interest Press Ctrl-Z to switch back to the map, if desired To put it simply: it’s a big deal. Conforming points into markers makes markers on the map feel a little bit more natural, and something that was desperately needed a bit further up. And now Ralc gains. While setting the marker and then editing that marked mark is still a hassle at this point, Sailfish Maps has removed a major friction. And we’re also now closer to fixing some of the design issues that caused this. In Summary We now have exactly what we were after: an interactive map system. Everything is completely operational and almost automatized for users now. We are just waiting to tie up a few minor loose ends to improve important details like the layout and visuals of the map markers (important for an interactive map system), and for the Mapnik and Ralc keyboard shortcuts to be more sensibly placed (we really want more users to know how to create and edit points in maps). We hope that all these technical and design issues will still be fixed when we arrive at the end of the feature itself in the future. One last thing I want to note before closing is that this is the Sailfish release. We still have much work left to do on making Sailfish into a great user experience, so I’ll hand this post to our primary Sailfish developer, Alex Hirsch.<|endoftext_R9VQqF0Ag7|>Selling Online Travel & Business Packages Business is a constantly evolving endeavor due to constant advancements in technologies and commerce. If you are anything like me, then your business has at times been travel or online business. Gain from travel can be one of the aspects businessmen try to master. Sell from online certainly has its own challenges, but the bottom line is effort can only be made! Starting up an online business is never simple or well thought out. The internet is coming to dominate as of now and playing an important role in achieving success and success of the business, but there is no definite method for successful business sales and package sale. Different tips for setting up an online business or selling travel packages can help you effective online sales and marketing strategies and also create promotional campaigns with the help of online marketing specialists. Here are some basic tips for business start 1. Clarification: It is important to make solid reasoning why you want to start a business. A great endeavor will always start with motivation. If you are planning to start online business by developing online platforms it is important to figure out Why you want start online rather than start in a shop? And at what point of time should you start an online business? These factors can vary from economy, to costs, bookkeeping, skills and passage of time. If you are ready to get over, or at least go over these challenges, you will thrive ever after. 2. Audience: It must go without saying, when you are planning to start an online travel business, you should take all kinds of strategies to see how target audience is expected to interact with your online business. It is important to view all of the information in order to get your most ideal audience into account. How you will expect customers to see your brand in positive or negative light? how regular can you expect traffic from and whether they are expected to come back to your primary site. 3. Pricing: These days we are worried about special discounts or high pricing when we come to pre-sales in promoting our ventures. It must go without saying, to first figure out what you are planning to and then to get all the related hype. Pitching is a way not only to attract customers and your target audience to your brand but also to larger sets of customers,"
